mantle rm203
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_olaf_stoneley
title the lid fiddler
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers talk=quiet temper=even
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk tests_small_sounds_with_a_tin_lid
likes plum_tart wrestling festival_bells thunder
dislikes early_bells drizzle
fears noise_covering_a_call
hopes a_box_of_sounds
topics pastimes +0.6 smalltalk +0.4 day +0.3 food +0.2 gossip -0.4
styles comfort=quiet gossip=spare refuse=level tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# listens from the edge of a crowd and gets a surprising range of noises from a dented tin lid, usually with a straight face.

words
oath! = Hot rivets and cold brine | Tongs in the breakers
saying! = Let the little noise finish | Turn a lid and the room changes
tin = my battered lid | the little tin disc
rim = the rolled lip | the bent edge
ding = a high thin note | a bright little ping
woolpad = folded wool | a scrap of felt
stick = my tapping twig | a dry sliver
plum = a baked plum | a pocket of plum jam
crust = the brown corner | the flaky rim
throw = a clean tumble | a sideways roll
slam = two boards clapping | a plank slapping stone
drip = the quietest drip | a slow bead falling
pause = the gap between strokes | a breath of silence
box = a narrow box | a shallow tray

any
opinion church for 1 : Best door in my book opens before anybody asks if you believe enough to come inside.
opinion dole for 2 : Hunger makes even a little noise hurt. Give a wolf something to chew first.
opinion merchants against 1 : I notice a short measure quicker than I notice a shiny sign.
opinion festivals mixed 1 : Plenty to listen to at a feast. I'd give the shouting a holiday too.
opinion city for 1 : Stone changes the sound every few steps here. You can travel with your ears.
opinion times against 1 [world.times=lean|hard] : The queue for a crust goes round the corner. An empty belly shouldn't have to walk that far.
any
line greet : Mind the lid underfoot. There's room beyond it. | Come round this side. I can hear you better.
line greet.return : Hello. I heard the tread before the voice. | Here I am, beside the wall.
line farewell.return : I'll keep the last bit of our talk. | Away with you, then. I'll hear your feet go.
line farewell : My ears will miss your company. | Till another quiet patch finds us.
line react.news : I need a quiet second with that news. | I heard the whole thing that time.
line react.news.new : That's the first I've caught of it. | You have my ears now.
line react.news.doubt : I'd give a witness my better ear. | A good echo can sound like another witness.
line react.news.known : That bit reached this corner already. | I could have tapped along to that telling.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'll put the lid away for a while. | Seems wrong to make a racket after hearing that.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice] : There's news that deserves a little ring. | That merits my finest little flourish.
line decline : I'd sooner stay here and finish listening. | Keep my turn for somebody with quicker feet.
line accept_decline : I'll count you out this round. | You can watch alongside me instead.
line accept_preclose : Go while the way's still clear. | I've had enough of your time already.
line preclose : I hear something over there I want to catch. | My little experiment will have to start soon.
line sympathise : You could sit by me without explaining any of it. | I'd have trouble swallowing that too.
line reassure : A bad sound dies out eventually. I'll wait beside you. | We'll take it a little piece at a time.
line ask.how : Anything been wearing on your ears lately? | Have you found yourself a minute of peace?
line answer.how : Steady as tin laid flat. | Quite content till somebody stamps nearby.
line thank : You left me time to say it. Thanks. | A quiet kindness, that. I heard it.
line deflect_thanks : Listen for somebody else when you can. | Plenty of room in a pause for two.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : I've saved you a corner where the voices carry. | Over here, past the loud bunch.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Family gets the good listening place. Step up. | Come by my shoulder. You know the drill.
line again.open : We've made a neat little circuit today. | Those footsteps came round again.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : I almost missed you in the dim. | A quiet voice carries far this late.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends] : Recognised the step. Good to see the rest of you. | My favourite interruption has arrived.

scene echo_test
when topic=pastimes|smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep #tin# for the noise, not the shine. | Sounds bigger if I hold it up here.
b : Where's the noise in it? | Does the height matter?
a : Touch #rim# with #stick#. There it is. | Try it against your belly. All you get is a thud.


scene dry_rim
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Rain plays a dent differently from flat tin. | A bead stuck on #rim#. See it shiver.
b : Does it change the note? | Going to tip it off?
a : On the flat it ticks. In the dent it gives a little grunt. | No, I want to see which drop sends it over.


scene crust_corner
when topic=food self.likes=plum_tart
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll cut a tart crooked if the corner's crisp. | I eat round the plum till there's an island left.
b : Doesn't somebody get a small slice? | And how do you pick up the island?
a : Mine. I like a thin bit of scorched crust. | With some ambition and a spoon.


scene holds
when topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I'd give a wrestler points for landing quietly. | I like a throw where both wolves get up laughing.
b : Then a soft patch of earth would win. | Less bruising that way.
a : Earth hasn't learned to throw yet. | I was thinking more of the sound.


scene tin_hearsay
when topic=gossip
does tell.gossip / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A rumour gets louder the farther it travels. Funny thing. | I could pass on a whole tale in three taps.
b : You sound doubtful. | What would the taps mean?
a : I am. Try shouting from the next street and see how far the truth carries. | Couldn't hear it. That's the whole tale from me.


scene two_seats
when topic=friends
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Sit just there and we'll hear different things. | I like a companion who leaves me a little quiet.
b : I'll pass on whatever reaches this ear. | Can I leave too much?
a : That's the best part. I only brought one pair of ears. | I'll tap twice if I need words.

grown

scene rest_lid
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put #woolpad# under things that rattle. | Set a cup down gently enough and it'll seem to land twice.
b : Even the tin? | Twice how?
a : Especially that. I want to choose when it speaks. | Once in your paw and once in your ear.


scene roof_talk
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Thunder makes all the little things stop rattling for a moment. | There's the loud roof voice again.
b : Really stop? | You're enjoying that.
a : Perhaps I just can't hear them. A difference worth listening for. | Better a roof that answers than one that lifts.


scene spare_shift
when topic=work self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A worn handle squeaks on every third twist. | I know a finished job by ear.
b : Why only the third? | Which sound gives it away?
a : That's when I change my grip. I took the handle's blame for it. | The first easy breath after the last hard one.


scene bent_note
when topic=lore|pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : If I knock the dent flat I'll lose this note. | Had a chance at an undented lid myself.
b : Better leave it crooked. | It sounds as if you passed.
a : I do. Nobody's ever offered to buy the dent. | I've got no use for a lid that sounds like every other lid.


scene still_news
when topic=newcomer
does give.opinion / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I let a newcomer choose how loud to speak. | The usual welcome is a great many questions at once.
b : What if you can't hear? | What would you change?
a : I can lean closer. That's my half of the welcome. | Leave a gap wide enough for one answer.


scene season_leaf
when topic=season here.season=autumn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : These leaves are turning the street into paper. | Hear that rustle under us.
b : I can hear every step. | You like that, do you?
a : I wonder who'll make the first quiet one. | Yes. The street usually keeps its opinions to itself.


scene hum_lip
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When my head rings I put #tin# down. | Ever heard a sound go on when the room is quiet?
b : Glad of a rest? | Does it bother you?
a : Mainly I'm trying to find which of us is ringing. | Less now I know I can wait it out.


scene gate_stone
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : On these steps I can tell stone from a loose board by ear. | The hill gives a shout a second little tail.
b : Do you shut your eyes to do it? | Where does it end?
a : Only after I've sat down safely. | At the next wall, unless someone there joins in.


scene cloth_gift
when topic=friends
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A square of wool is a fine present if you know what rattles. | I wouldn't wrap a gift in tin.
b : Might need explaining. | Too loud for a surprise?
a : I can demonstrate in one tap. | Too tempting to keep the wrapper myself.


scene quiet_prayer
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My lips scarcely move, even over a prayer. | I wait for the last footstep before I pray.
b : Even after good news? | Does it help?
a : Especially then. Good news can make a fair din without me. | I can finish a thought without mistaking it for somebody else's.


scene sleeping_tools
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dreamt of a forge that beat like a surf line. | In my dream the sea had a lid.
b : How did the smith keep up? | Who lifted it?
a : Slept through the whole shift. Dream forges can run themselves. | Nobody. That's how I knew I'd overslept.


scene share_sound
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Lend me an ear for one tap. | A tap's easy enough to miss.
b : Where do you want me? | You reckon I missed one?
a : Behind the board. Listen for what reaches you first, wood or tin. | Yes. That smile means you caught the second.

young

scene lesson_game
when topic=pastimes|day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've made a game you can play without moving from this step. | Pick a noise and keep it secret.
b : Have I already started? | How will you know if I'm right?
a : Yes. Next cart through, count the squeaks. | When it comes again, point. I'll point as well.


scene pot_band
when topic=pastimes|friends
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My band has one lid and no pay. | I need a musician whose whole part is keeping still.
b : What's the band called? | I could manage that.
a : Late for supper. We finish our whole programme in four taps. | Lovely. You've learnt the hard bit.


scene lesson_crump
when topic=day self.job=child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I made the chalk squeak at lessons and nearly bit my tongue. | My slate's quiet now. I've found the trick.
b : Were you trying not to laugh? | A softer chalk?
a : Yes. The chalk sounded more surprised than the teacher. | No. Wrote the sums with the right end.


scene school_prize
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : If there were prizes for keeping quiet I'd have a shelf full. | My dream is a cupboard of tiny sounds.
b : You'd have to say thank you. | Mightn't they escape?
a : There goes my prize. | That's what the lid's for.


scene puddle_ring
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm holding #tin# out till a drop hits dead centre. | My ears can tell when drizzle gets serious.
b : What's the prize if it does? | Which part tells you?
a : I get to take it in. My arm's aching. | The cold bit underneath my fur.

adolescent

scene learned_tune
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can play a tune on three cups now. | I found a fourth note by accident.
b : Is it one I know? | Can you do it again?
a : You'll know it if I remember the middle. | Only if I drop the cup again. I quite like the cup.


scene proper_bout
when topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling
does tell.plan / react.self / assess
a : I want a bout where neither of us has to boast. | I'll wrestle if nobody's keeping score.
b : How will you know when to stop? | Won't you want to know who won?
a : When one of us asks. That's how I'd like to be treated. | I'll be close enough to tell.

any

story blanket_band [topic=memories]
  : I once folded a blanket over some tin so I could practise quietly. One layer swallowed high notes. Two swallowed low ones.
  : By the third I had a splendid silent concert under way.
  b : Was there an audience?
  : A sleeping one. Best review I could have hoped for.


story borrowed_step [topic=smalltalk]
  : I drummed a marching pace on my knee and a beetle came over to listen.
  : I halved the pace. The beetle carried on across my knee without me.
  b : Didn't take direction well.
  : Only musician I've met with a proper reason to walk offstage.


story pit_rattle [topic=food]
  : The stone came out of a plum and stuck in a seam of my pocket.
  : I washed the pocket and wore it twice before I found out what was rattling at me.
  b : You kept the stone, didn't you?
  : My coat had learned how to play. I wasn't going to spoil that.


rule @rimcry
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Hush a breath. The tin hasn't finished yet. | Last note's the little one. Wait for it.


rule @faircry
when concept=bark here.day=festival
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That's a proper festival clang! The tin agrees. | Bells like those could get a lid dancing.


rule @raincry
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Drop on the lip, plop in the middle. | Water's practising scales on my lid.


rule @supcry
when concept=bark self.likes=plum_tart
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Save the smallest slice with the burnt edge! | Nobody wants that crooked crust? Excellent.

dlg resident.hub : Give me a second to still this rattle. There, I'm listening.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, come hear what the lid does today.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : Voices carry nicely in the dark. You needn't raise yours.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I'd prefer to hear you from right where you stand.
dlg resident.job [self.job=child] : Lessons. I can usually tell which slate's going to squeak.
dlg resident.job : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. Ask me again once my ears have had a rest.
dlg resident.bye : Take some quiet with you if there's any left.
graft resident.hub
choice What does the dent do to the sound? -> rim_dent
node rim_dent
say It makes two notes argue. Catch the edge gently and you can hear the lower one win.
free
choice Can I try tapping it? -> rim_stroke
choice I'll listen instead. -> hub
node rim_stroke
say Use the side of your claw. Tap it flat and all you hear is your own tap.
choice I heard the second note. -> hub
choice I'll leave you to it. -> bye
